BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:General Conference Reflection Assignment (F/W) [REL C 333-033]
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261010
DTSTAMP:20261026T204400Z
UID:event-assignment-1441133
SEQUENCE:0
CLASS:PUBLIC
DESCRIPTION:[] (https://byu.instructure.com/courses/35044/files/13505106/p
 review?hidden=1)\n\nEstimated time: 40 minutes\n\nNote: Because this is a
  Living Prophets class\, general conference is an important highlight of o
 ur semester\; therefore\, this assignment is worth twice the value of othe
 r units’ assignments.\n\nThe content of this assignment will be your ref
 lections on the addresses from the most recent general conference of the C
 hurch.\n\nYou will answer the following questions thoughtfully\, drawing u
 pon your own experience participating in [general conference (Links to a
 n external site.)] (http://gc.churchofjesuschrist.org/)\; you may refer to
  notes or review any of the talks that are available online. Respond to ea
 ch question with a solid paragraph (minimum 3–4 sentences).\n\n* What th
 emes and repetition did you notice during this general conference?\n\n* Su
 mmarize briefly what stood out to you from President Oaks’s talks or ann
 ouncements or communications during general conference. (On an upcoming ex
 am\, you’ll be asked to analyze his general session talk more deeply.)\n
 \n* Identify a promised blessing and what you need to do to obtain it from
  President Eyring’s general session talk\, and share your main takeaway 
 from his message.\n\n* Identify a promised blessing and what you need to d
 o to obtain it from President Christofferson’s general session talk\, an
 d share your main takeaway from his message.\n\n* Choose one of the foll
 owing to answer:\n\n* Comment briefly on the talk by the apostle from your
  apostle paper. How did your preparation affect your reception of his mess
 age\, and what did you notice?\n\n* Comment on any experience you had find
 ing answers to questions or receiving what Elder Holland called “a perso
 nal prophetic epistle just to you.”[1] (#end) (You may be as specific o
 r general as you feel comfortable sharing.)\n\n* Did you watch (or listen 
 to) at least four general sessions of general conference? Yes/No: No parag
 raph is necessary. If no\, please indicate how much you completed.\n\n----
 -----------------------------\nRequirements for this assignment:\n--------
 -------------------------\n\n* title (“General Conference Reflections”
 ) and your name at the top\n\n* 2–3 pages total\n\n* 12-point Times New 
 Roman font\n\n* double spaced\n\n* one-inch margins\n\n* .doc\, .docx\, or
  .pdf format\n\nSubmission Instructions\n-----------------------\n\nWhen y
 ou are ready to upload and submit this assignment:\n\n* Click Submit Assig
 nment in the top-right corner.\n\n* Attach the relevant assignment by cli
 cking the Choose File button\, then locating the file you wish to submit
 .\n\n* When you are finished\, click Submit Assignment.\n\n* You should r
 eceive a message in the top-right corner telling you your assignment was t
 urned in.\n\nRubric: \n--------\n\nYou will earn 5 points for watching fo
 ur+ sessions of general conference and 3 points each for the content and r
 equirements of paragraphs 1–5.\n\nModule Item Completion (built in brows
 er\, hidden in app)\n\n----------\nReferences\n----------\n\n1 Jeffrey R. 
 Holland\, “[An Ensign to the Nations] (https://www.churchofjesuschrist.o
 rg/study/ensign/2011/05/sunday-afternoon-session/an-ensign-to-the-nations?
 lang=eng)\,” Ensign or Liahona\, May 2011.
URL;VALUE=URI:https://byu.instructure.com/calendar?include_contexts=course
 _35044&month=10&year=2026#assignment_1441133
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<link rel="stylesheet" href="https://instruct
 ure-uploads.s3.amazonaws.com/account_74070000000000001/attachments/8409020
 /dp_app.css"><link rel="stylesheet" href="https://instructure-uploads.s3.a
 mazonaws.com/account_74070000000000001/attachments/14123348/canvas-byu-byu
 online-mobile.css"><p><img src="https://byu.instructure.com/courses/35044/
 files/13505106/preview?hidden=1" alt="" width="2389" height="554" data-dec
 orative="true" data-api-endpoint="https://byu.instructure.com/api/v1/cours
 es/35044/files/13505106" data-api-returntype="File" loading="lazy"></p>\n<
 p><em><span style="font-size: 10pt\;">Estimated time: 40 minutes</span></e
 m></p>\n<p><strong>Note:</strong><span>&nbsp\;</span>Because this is a Liv
 ing Prophets class\, general conference is an important highlight of our s
 emester\; therefore\, this assignment is worth twice the value of other un
 its’ assignments.</p>\n<p>The content of this assignment will be your re
 flections on the addresses from the most recent general conference of the 
 Church.</p>\n<p>You will answer the following questions thoughtfully\, dra
 wing upon your own experience participating in<span>&nbsp\;</span><a class
 ="external" href="http://gc.churchofjesuschrist.org/" target="_blank"><spa
 n>general conference</span><span class="screenreader-only">&nbsp\;(Links t
 o an external site.)</span></a>\; you may refer to notes or review any of 
 the talks that are available online. Respond to each question with a solid
  paragraph (minimum 3–4 sentences).</p>\n<ol>\n<li>What themes and repet
 ition did you notice during this general conference?</li>\n<li>Summarize b
 riefly what stood out to you from President Oaks’s talks or announcement
 s or communications during general conference. (On an upcoming exam\, you
 ’ll be asked to analyze his general session talk more deeply.)</li>\n<li
 >Identify a promised blessing and what you need to do to obtain it from Pr
 esident Eyring’s general session talk\, and share your main takeaway fro
 m his message.</li>\n<li>Identify a promised blessing and what you need to
  do to obtain it from President Christofferson’s general session talk\, 
 and share your main takeaway from his message.</li>\n<li>Choose<span>&nbsp
 \;</span><span>one</span><span>&nbsp\;</span>of the following to answer:\n
 <ol type="A">\n<li>Comment briefly on the talk by the apostle from your ap
 ostle paper. How did your preparation affect your reception of his message
 \, and what did you notice?</li>\n<li>Comment on any experience you had fi
 nding answers to questions or receiving what Elder Holland called “a per
 sonal prophetic epistle just to you.”<a href="#end"><sup>1</sup></a><spa
 n>&nbsp\;</span>(You may be as specific or general as you feel comfortable
  sharing.)</li>\n</ol>\n</li>\n<li>Did you watch (or listen to) at least f
 our general sessions of general conference? Yes/No: No paragraph is necess
 ary. If no\, please indicate how much you completed.</li>\n</ol>\n<h2>Requ
 irements for this assignment:</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>title (“General Conference
  Reflections”) and your name at the top</li>\n<li><strong>2–3 pages to
 tal</strong></li>\n<li>12-point Times New Roman font</li>\n<li>double spac
 ed</li>\n<li>one-inch margins</li>\n<li>.doc\, .docx\, or .pdf format</li>
 \n</ul>\n<h3><strong>Submission Instructions</strong></h3>\n<p>When you ar
 e ready to upload and submit this assignment:</p>\n<ol>\n<li>Click Submit 
 Assignment in the top-right corner.</li>\n<li>Attach&nbsp\;the relevant as
 signment by clicking the&nbsp\;Choose File&nbsp\;button\, then locating th
 e file you wish to submit.</li>\n<li>When you are finished\, click&nbsp\;S
 ubmit Assignment.</li>\n<li>You should receive a message in the top-right 
 corner telling you your assignment was turned in.</li>\n</ol>\n<h3>\n<stro
 ng>Rubric:</strong><span>&nbsp\;</span>\n</h3>\n<p>You will earn 5 points 
 for watching four+ sessions of general conference and 3 points each for th
 e content and requirements of paragraphs 1–5.</p>\n<p class="kl_module_p
 rogress_completion" style="display: none\;">Module Item Completion (built 
 in browser\, hidden in app)</p>\n<div id="kl_custom_block_0" class="kl_pan
 els_wrapper kl_panels_expander kl_no_expander_controls">\n<h2 id="kl_panel
 _0" class="kl_panel_heading kl_panel_0"><span style="font-size: 14pt\;">Re
 ferences</span></h2>\n<div id="kl_panel_0_content" class="kl_panel_content
  kl_panel_0">\n<p><sup>1</sup> Jeffrey R. Holland\, “<a href="https://ww
 w.churchofjesuschrist.org/study/ensign/2011/05/sunday-afternoon-session/an
 -ensign-to-the-nations?lang=eng">An Ensign to the Nations</a>\,” <em>Ens
 ign</em> or <em>Liahona</em>\, May 2011.</p>\n</div>\n</div>\n<hr id="end"
  style="height: 4px\; background-color: #002e5d\; color: #002e5d\;"><scrip
