BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Proclamations Analysis [REL C 333-033]
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261024
DTSTAMP:20261025T230000Z
UID:event-assignment-1441142
SEQUENCE:0
CLASS:PUBLIC
DESCRIPTION:[] (https://byu.instructure.com/courses/35044/files/13505106/p
 review?hidden=1)\n\nEstimated time: 45 minutes\n\nThis is an opportunity t
 o share what you learned from your study of the proclamations and the rela
 ted talks. \n\nYou will receive points for addressing the assigned topics
  below in five very short paragraphs. Each should be 3–4 sentences but s
 hould show thought and preparation\, demonstrating an understanding of the
  information asked for. Do not quote from the sources\; summarize the conc
 epts in your own words.\n\nYou may be tempted to write a longer paper\, bu
 t I want you to keep it right around one page\; just focus on the main poi
 nts and write clear summaries of those principles. Consider each question/
 paragraph to be a short-answer question.\n\nParagraph 1: What did you see 
 in the proclamations studied in this lesson that showed evidence of the au
 thors’ roles as prophets\, seers\, and revelators? (Share 2–3 examples
 .)\n\nParagraph 2: When you did your organizational analysis of the family
  proclamation\, what overarching categories did you choose to focus on\, a
 nd what were some of the subcategories you identified for each one?\n\nPar
 agraph 3: Summarize the meaning/message of The Living Christ in one senten
 ce. Then comment on what stood out to you and/or what you learned about Je
 sus Christ.\n\nParagraph 4: How does the content in the Restoration Procla
 mation support the claim in its first sentence? What principles in the pro
 clamation most inspired gratitude as you studied it?\n\nParagraph 5: Share
  some of your own thoughts and feelings as you studied these proclamations
  and the lesson content. What did you feel was your personal call to actio
 n?\n\nOptional Question: These proclamations focus on doctrines that are f
 undamental to the Church of Jesus Christ of Latter-day Saints. Do you have
  any questions you’d like to ask me (your instructor)\, or is there anyt
 hing you’d like to discuss further?\n\nRequirements for this essay inclu
 de the following:\n\n* title (“Proclamations Analysis”) and your name 
 at the top\n\n* one page (up to one and a half pages)\n\n* 12-point Times 
 New Roman font\n\n* double spaced\n\n* one-inch margins\n\n* .doc\, .docx
 \, or .pdf format\n\nSubmission Instructions\n\nWhen you are ready to uplo
 ad and submit this assignment:\n\n* Click Submit Assignment in the top-r
 ight corner.\n\n* Attach the relevant assignment by clicking the Choose 
 File button\, then locating the file you wish to submit.\n\n* When you ar
 e finished\, click Submit Assignment.\n\n* You should receive a message i
 n the top-right corner telling you that your assignment was submitted.\n\n
 Rubric: You will earn up to 2 points for fulfilling content and requiremen
 ts of each paragraph.\n\nModule Item Completion (built in browser\, hidden
  in app)
URL;VALUE=URI:https://byu.instructure.com/calendar?include_contexts=course
 _35044&month=10&year=2026#assignment_1441142
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<link rel="stylesheet" href="https://instruct
 ure-uploads.s3.amazonaws.com/account_74070000000000001/attachments/8409020
 /dp_app.css"><link rel="stylesheet" href="https://instructure-uploads.s3.a
 mazonaws.com/account_74070000000000001/attachments/14123348/canvas-byu-byu
 online-mobile.css"><p><img src="https://byu.instructure.com/courses/35044/
 files/13505106/preview?hidden=1" alt="" width="2389" height="554" data-dec
 orative="true" data-api-endpoint="https://byu.instructure.com/api/v1/cours
 es/35044/files/13505106" data-api-returntype="File" loading="lazy"></p>\n<
 p><em><span style="font-size: 10pt\;">Estimated time: 45 minutes</span></e
 m></p>\n<p>This is an opportunity to share what you learned from your stud
 y of the proclamations and the related talks.&nbsp\;</p>\n<p>You will rece
 ive points for addressing the assigned topics below in five <strong>very s
 hort</strong> paragraphs. Each should be 3–4 sentences but should show t
 hought and preparation\, demonstrating an understanding of the information
  asked for. Do not quote from the sources\; summarize the concepts in your
  own words.</p>\n<p><em>You may be tempted to write a longer paper\, but I
  want you to keep it right around one page\; just focus on the main points
  and write clear summaries of those principles. Consider each question/par
 agraph to be a short-answer question.</em></p>\n<p><strong>Paragraph 1:</s
 trong> What did you see in the proclamations studied in this lesson that s
 howed evidence of the authors’ roles as prophets\, seers\, and revelator
 s? (Share 2–3 examples.)</p>\n<p><strong>Paragraph 2:</strong> When you 
 did your organizational analysis of the family proclamation\, what overarc
 hing categories did you choose to focus on\, and what were some of the sub
 categories you identified for each one?</p>\n<p><strong>Paragraph 3:</stro
 ng><span> Summarize the meaning/message of <em>The Living Christ</em> in o
 ne sentence. Then comment on what stood out to you and/or what you learned
  about Jesus Christ.</span></p>\n<p><strong>Paragraph 4:</strong> How does
  the content in the Restoration Proclamation support the claim in its firs
 t sentence? What principles in the proclamation most inspired gratitude as
  you studied it?</p>\n<p><strong>Paragraph 5:</strong> Share some of your 
 own thoughts and feelings as you studied these proclamations and the lesso
 n content. What did you feel was your personal call to action?</p>\n<p><em
 ><strong>Optional Question</strong>:</em> <span>These proclamations focus 
 on doctrines that are fundamental to the Church of Jesus Christ of Latter-
 day Saints. Do you have any questions you’d like to ask me (your instruc
 tor)\, or is there anything you’d like to discuss further?</span></p>\n<
 p>Requirements for this essay include the following:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>title 
 (“Proclamations Analysis”) and your name at the top</li>\n<li>one page
  (up to one and a half pages)</li>\n<li>12-point Times New Roman font</li>
 \n<li>double spaced</li>\n<li>one-inch margins</li>\n<li>.doc\, .docx\, or
  .pdf format</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Submission Instructions</strong></p>
 \n<p>When you are ready to upload and submit this assignment:</p>\n<ol>\n<
 li>Click&nbsp\;<strong>Submit Assignment&nbsp\;</strong>in the top-right c
 orner.</li>\n<li>Attach&nbsp\;the relevant assignment by clicking the&nbsp
 \;<strong>Choose File</strong>&nbsp\;button\, then locating the file you w
 ish to submit.</li>\n<li>When you are finished\, click&nbsp\;<strong>Submi
 t Assignment</strong>.</li>\n<li>You should receive a message in the top-r
 ight corner telling you that your assignment was submitted.</li>\n</ol>\n<
 p><strong>Rubric:</strong> You will earn up to 2 points for fulfilling con
 tent and requirements of each paragraph.</p>\n<p class="kl_module_progress
 _completion" style="display: none\;">Module Item Completion (built in brow
