SUMMARY:Uchtdorf and Bednar Questions Assignment [REL C 333-033]
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261031
DTSTAMP:20261024T060000Z
UID:event-assignment-1441101
SEQUENCE:0
CLASS:PUBLIC
DESCRIPTION:[] (https://byu.instructure.com/courses/35044/files/13505106/d
 ownload?hidden=1)\n\nEstimated time: 30 minutes\n\nFor this small-group di
 scussion\, you will make two posts by responding to these prompts:\n\n* In
  President Uchtdorf’s talk\, “The Adventure of Mortality\,” he asked
  twenty-one different questions (look at all the question marks)\, and he 
 also talked about questions. Choose one question from Elder Uchtdorf’s t
 alk and comment briefly (3–4 sentences) with your thoughts or lessons le
 arned about that question as you studied his talk. Then\, at the end of yo
 ur paragraph\, ask your classmates a question inspired by any of the Presi
 dent Uchtdorf or Elder Bednar talks you read for this lesson. It can be on
  any related topic\, but pick something you’d really like to hear anothe
 r student’s thoughts about. Try to be specific and invite a thoughtful r
 esponse.\n\n* After he gave his devotional “A Welding Link\,” Elder Be
 dnar made a post on Twitter in which he repeated an important question. [W
 atch the short video in his tweet] (https://t.co/ig42M4nPiy) ([David A. Be
 dnar Video Tweet Transcript] (https://byu.instructure.com/courses/35044/fi
 les/13505600?wrap=1)) to see some of the answers he received. (You may nee
 d to unmute the volume in the bottom right corner of the video.) Create yo
 ur own video response to Elder Bednar’s “Welding Link” Twitter invit
 ation and video. Describe how you will be a welding link in your own famil
 y. (Keep it Twitter-sized: 30–60 seconds is fine.)\n\nTo complete #2\, y
 ou will record directly in Canvas. This is done simply by replying to this
  assignment. Detailed steps are listed below. Since it's such a short vide
 o\, uploading it to Canvas should not be a problem\, but if you have troub
 le\, you can alternatively check [Resources for Creating Videos] (https://
 byu.instructure.com/courses/35044/pages/resources-for-creating-videos).\n
 \n[Screenshot guiding to record/upload media.] (https://byu.instructure.co
 m/courses/35044/files/13505476/download?hidden=1)\n\n*\n\nClick the Reply 
 button directly below this assignment description.\n\n* At the top of the 
 comment box\, there is an icon that says “Record/Upload Media” when yo
 u hover over it. It is the button directly to the left of the paragraph sy
 mbols.\n\n*\n\nWhen you click this icon\, a pop-up box will appear where y
 ou can see whether your video and audio are functioning. Check both before
  proceeding.\n\n*\n\nWhen you are ready to begin recording\, hit the Recor
 d button.\n\n*\n\nTo finish your recording\, simply click the Finish butto
 n.\n\n*\n\nClicking the Save button will automatically upload* your video 
 to the comment box.\n\n*\n\nAfter the video icon appears in the comment bo
 x\, click the Post Reply button to publish your comment and video to the d
 iscussion.\n\n* Note: It may take a minute or so for your video to upload.
  The longer your recording\, the longer it takes to save and appear on the
  screen. You could also record it separately on your phone or other device
  and then upload it instead of recording it within the comment box\, but f
 ile size is limited (up to 500 MB). In either case\, keep it short and sim
 ple.\n\nReplies: Reply thoughtfully to another student’s video and answe
 r one student’s question. You may watch and read as many as you want\, b
 ut you are only required to respond to one video and one question. You can
  choose specific posts\, or look for some that have not yet received a res
 ponse.\n\nYour posts and replies are due by the date indicated at the top 
 of this discussion. This is a small-group discussion\, so please participa
 te in a timely manner as other students will be awaiting your response.\n
 \nRubric: You will earn up to 4 points for your Uchtdorf reflections and q
 uestion\, 4 points for your Bednar video response\, and 2 points for reply
 ing to peers (answering one question and replying to one video response). 
 To see the complete rubric\, click on the three dots in the top right corn
 er of this page. Then click "Show Rubric."\n\nModule Item Completion (buil
 t in browser\, hidden in app)
